{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_155901_239d50", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Q1. **Yes, you can upgrade the memory yourself.** The documentation states in **Section 2: Memory and Storage Upgrades** that \"Customers may upgrade memory themselves.\" It also notes that the device has two SO-DIMM memory slots supporting up to 128 GB.\n\nQ2. **Standard warranty is 3 years on-site, next-business-day.** You can extend it to 4 or 5 years **at purchase or within 90 days of purchase**, as stated in **Section 1: Warranty and Support**. Accidental damage protection is sold separately.\n\nQ3. **You can run up to three external 4K displays at 60 Hz from one Thunderbolt 5 dock**, or two external displays at up to 8K 60 Hz. This is covered in **Section 3: Docking and External Displays**.\n\nQ4. **If the BIOS is corrupted or attacked, the system automatically restores a protected copy at the next boot.** This is described in **Section 4: Security Features**, which mentions the \"self-healing BIOS\" that continuously checks firmware integrity.\n\nQ5. **Not covered in the provided documentation.** The documentation lists Ubuntu 24.04 as a potential question but does not confirm certification status. The customer should contact customer support or check the official Aurora 14 compatibility list.", "tokens": {"input": 575, "output": 282, "total": 4676, "cache_read": 3819, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 35026, "timestamp": 1790809176227}